{# THE AREA OVERVIEW — what is happening in this area right now, composed from
   every module installed here.

   Design: areas/<area>/index.html and overview.widgets.js.

   THE AREA PAGE OWNS THE SURFACE AND WRITES NONE OF THE OPERATIONAL CONTENT. The
   identity band below is this bundle's, because an area's size and gazettement
   are what an area IS. Everything else on the page is contributed: the tiles in
   the right-now strip, the rows in "Needs attention", the layers on the map. A
   module installed in this area puts them there; uninstall it and they leave.

   ABSENT IS NOT ZERO, EVERYWHERE. A strip nobody contributed to is not drawn at
   all — it is not drawn full of noughts, which would claim six measurements
   nobody took. An empty attention list is a good day, and a good day is allowed
   to look like one.

   NO WIDGET INDICES. The design file prints one in each plate's tab (AO·04,
   PL·N1); that is the workspace's referencing system and not product. See
   tests/Unit/Template/NoWorkshopLabelsTest.php. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }}{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
    {# AND EACH CONTRIBUTING MODULE'S OWN SHEET, once and last. A module's
       cell is drawn here and its rules live in its own package; without this
       the cell renders with every class it wrote undefined, which is how an
       incident cell's flow bar came out as blue underlined links. Last, so a
       module may tune what it owns — and only what it owns: the page's own
       vocabulary is the area's and restating it is caught by the sheet
       tests, here as everywhere. #}
    {% for sheet in moduleStylesheets %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(sheet) }}">
    {% endfor %}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">areas</a> / {{ area.name }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }}{% endblock %}

{# ONE LINE: what THIS tab is for. The strip says which tab you are on, and
   a subline that wrapped pushed the whole page down by a line's height. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}What is happening in this area right now, composed from every module installed here.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {# THE PAGE IS COMPOSED, NOT AUTHORED.

       Everything below is resolved from the person's active preset over the
       catalogue this area assembled: the area's own cells, and one cell from
       every module switched on here. This template names no module, knows no
       module's numbers and contains no widget markup — uninstalling a module
       removes its cell from the grid and its widget from the library, and a
       saved preset that named it degrades rather than breaking.

       THE SPAN IS THE CELL'S OWN, from the catalogue: twelve for the things
       that are about the whole area, six for the pair of cards that read
       side by side. #}
    <div class="w-grid">
        {% for cell in cells %}
            <div class="w-cell w-span-{{ cell.cols }}">
                {# ONE MAP, AND NOT THE PAGE'S CONTEXT. A contributed cell is
                   rendered `with_context: false` and reads its own figures
                   under `by.<slug>` — the contract every module template is
                   written against. Handing the page's variables instead
                   would work for the host's own cells and fatal on every
                   module's, which is exactly what it did. #}
                {{ include(partials[cell.id], cellContext, with_context: false) }}
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
